# live-xdp-fleet.inventory.example -- placeholder hosts only.
#
# One row per machine, whitespace separated, in this order:
#
#   label  ssh-name  role  shape  site  path  cap-kbps  nic  address  queues
#
#   label     the bench label on every result line; never a hostname
#   ssh-name  the name ssh uses, from the coordinator's machine
#   role      server or client
#   shape     linux, windows-interop or macos (the bench's build and start shape)
#   site      studio or datacenter (the site that sets the cap)
#   path      lan or internet; this run is the internet path
#   cap-kbps  the client's total cap, both directions combined (the byte budget
#             stated in scripts/live-xdp-fleet):
#             1000 for a studio-site client, 100000 for a datacenter client.
#             The server row carries its own site's maximum and is not a
#             client cap.
#   nic       the server row's public NIC; "-" on a client row
#   address   the server row's public IPv4 and UDP port; "-" on a client row
#   queues    the server row's XDP queue count; "-" on a client row
#
# The real inventory lives outside the repository and is named by
# ROCKETNET_LIVE_INVENTORY. Replace every .invalid name before a run.
#
# The example is the owner's shape: seven
# studio-site clients at 1 Mbit/s total and two datacenter clients at
# 100 Mbit/s total, which is about 0.54 GB across the studio uplink and
# about 16.07 GB in all, inside the 1 GB and 20 GB bounds of the byte budget.

# label            ssh-name                    role    shape            site        path      cap-kbps  nic   address           queues
test-server      test-server.invalid         server  linux            datacenter  internet  100000    eth0  192.0.2.10:40000  8
studio-linux-1   studio-linux-1.invalid      client  linux            studio      internet  1000      -     -                 -
studio-linux-2   studio-linux-2.invalid      client  linux            studio      internet  1000      -     -                 -
studio-win-1     studio-win-1.invalid        client  windows-interop  studio      internet  1000      -     -                 -
studio-win-2     studio-win-2.invalid        client  windows-interop  studio      internet  1000      -     -                 -
studio-macos-1   studio-macos-1.invalid      client  macos            studio      internet  1000      -     -                 -
studio-macos-2   studio-macos-2.invalid      client  macos            studio      internet  1000      -     -                 -
studio-linux-3   studio-linux-3.invalid      client  linux            studio      internet  1000      -     -                 -
dc-linux-1       dc-linux-1.invalid          client  linux            datacenter  internet  100000    -     -                 -
dc-linux-2       dc-linux-2.invalid          client  linux            datacenter  internet  100000    -     -                 -
